class_name Salts
extends RefCounted
## Every salt the game deals by, in one list (docs/CODE_REVIEW.md 2.4). What is dealt without the
## world RNG is a hash of a seed and a salt (Rules.level_seed(seed, salt), RisoDecor.h): two rules
## that salt the same seed with the same number are not two deals but one, so no two salts may be
## alike. Each is given its number here by its place in the list, and where it is used it is that
## number times STRIDE (`const KEY_DEAL: int = Salts.SHRINE_KEY * Salts.STRIDE`), so what a rule
## adds to its salt (a cell's x * 977 + y, a try's count) does not walk it onto the next one's.
## A new salt goes at the END of the list: one put in the middle moves every salt after it, and
## with them everything those deal, in every level (layout_fingerprint_test says so). unit_test
## checks that every salt in the scripts is from this list and that none is used by two constants.

## How far apart two salts' numbers are: more than a rule adds to its own within a level.
const STRIDE: int = 1000003

## The salts, named for the script and the constant that deals by each.
